# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository, always.
#
# Without this, an editor or tool on Windows can rewrite every file to CRLF and
# produce a diff where every file appears fully changed - 24,996 insertions and
# 24,996 deletions, with zero content difference. That diff looks like real work,
# is not, and committing it would destroy `git blame` across the whole repo.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide which files are text; `eol=lf` fixes what goes into
# the repository. Working-tree endings on Windows are unaffected for tools that
# care.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must stay byte-exact regardless of platform.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
